<newsitem itemid="613456" id="root" date="1997-05-26" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Absa lifts year earnings and dividend.</title>
<headline>Absa lifts year earnings and dividend.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)	222.2	   vs 178.0</p>
<p>    Shr, net (cts)	     222.2	   vs 196.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    72.0	    vs 59.0</p>
<p>    Net income		   1,319	   vs 1,130</p>
<p>    Net pre-exceptionals     1,964	   vs 1,564</p>
<p>    Net interest income	5,313	   vs 4,616</p>
<p>    Other operating income   3,283	   vs 2,503</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge   766	   vs   538</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			1,964	   vs 1,695</p>
<p>    Tax				666	   vs   591</p>
<p>Div payable July 23</p>
<p>On register June 13</p>
<p>Full name: Amalgamated Banks of South Africa Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it would offer shareholder capitalisation shares in lieu of the cash dividend.</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast EPS of 225.5 with the range 223.0-228.8 and a dividend of 73.1 with the range 70.8-75.5.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
